1 _OID 02099531-9632-43f2-af42-65847bed375c
1 DATE 1926 - 2005
1 PLAC Lafourche Parish, Louisiana, USA
1 _DSCR Obituary
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Roy R. Angelette Sr., 79, a native of Golden Meadow and resident of Larose, died Monday, October 3, 2005. Visitation will be from 4 to 10 p.m. Wednesday and from 8 a.m. to funeral time Thursday at Falgout Funeral Home i
2 CONC n Galliano. Mass will be at 11 a.m. Thursday at Our Lady of the Rosary Catholic Church in Larose, with burial in the church cemetery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He is survived by his wife, Rose Mary Savoie Angelette; three sons and daughters-in-law, Roy &a
2 CONC mp;quot;Bobby&amp;quot; Angelette Jr. and wife, Barbara, Ronnie Angelette and wife, Denise, and Keith Angelette and wife, Donna; one daughter and son-in-law, Crystal Redmond and husband, Price; one son-in-law, Kurt Eschette; two brothers and sister
2 CONC s-in-law, Ambert Angelette Jr. and wife, Geneveive and Steve Angelette and wife, Carolyn; two sisters and brothers-in-law, Natalie Toups and husband, George, and Lorraine Eymard and husband, Roger Sr.; one sister, Eloise Cheramie; and his grandchil
2 CONC dren, their spouses and his great-grandchildren, Neil and Tracy Angelette and their children, Natalie, Nicholas and Mark, Mignon and Stephen Gill and their child, Alexandra, Brandy and Jamie Cheramie and their children, Kurstan and Karoline, Mathe
2 CONC w Eschette, Cody and Jera Angelette and their child, Haiven, Domonique Angelette, Heather Eschette, Kristen Angelette, Michael Redmond, Shelby Angelette, Ryan Redmond and Nicole Redmond.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was preceded in death by his parents, A
2 CONC mbert Angelette Sr. and Natalie Angelette; one daughter, Patsy Angelette Eschette; one sister and brother-in-law, Yvonne and Wendel Harvey; and one brother-in-law, Harrison Cheramie Jr.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was founder of A.Angelette and Sons Cons
2 CONC truction Co.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was a hard-working cattleman and enjoyed spending time with his wife and family. He was a member of the Lafourche Cattlemen&amp;rsquo;s Association and the VFW.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was a U.S. World War II Navy v
2 CONC eteran, proudly serving in the Pacific as a Higgins Landing Craft Operator and Instructor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Published in &amp;quot;The Houma Courier&amp;quot; on October 4. 2005.&amp;nbsp; </line></content></metadataxml>
