2 CONC ; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;George Earl Toups, 82, a native of Golden Meadow and resident of Galliano, died at 1:16 p.m. Wednesda
2 CONC y, Jan. 20, 2010.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div style="margin: 0px 0px 20px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-family: georgia, serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 23.885000228881836px; word-spacing: 2px;"&gt;<
2 CONC /line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0px 0px 1em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;Visitation will be from 5 to 9 p.m. today at Falgout Fune
2 CONC ral Home in Galliano. Mass will be 11 a.m. Friday at St. Joseph Catholic Church, with burial in the church cemetery.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0px 0px 1em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style
2 CONC : inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;He is survived by three sons, Clark Anthony Toups Sr. and wife, Lois, Buddy Toups Sr. and wife, Carolyn, and Gene Toups and wife, Pamela; seven grandchildren; and eight great-g
2 CONC randchildren.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0px 0px 1em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;He was preceded in death by his p
2 CONC arents, Edmund and Maude Jeandron Toups; one great-grandchild, Trey Mikeal Toups; five brothers, Walden Toups, Lester Toups, John Toups, Jules Toups and Raymond Toups; and four sisters, Winnie Pitre, Mildred Watson, Elsie Byrd and Anna Mae Pitre.&l
2 CONC t;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0px 0px 1em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;He was a parishioner of St. Joseph Catholic Chur
2 CONC ch. He was a corporal in the sixth Marine division. He was a lifetime member of the V.F.W. 8538 and the Golden Meadow American Legion 259.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0px 0px 1em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-weight
2 CONC : inherit; font-style: inherit; font-family: inherit; line-height: 25.290000915527344px;"&gt;Falgout Funeral Home is in charge of arrangements.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
