2 CONC ;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;3&lt;span&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font color="#003399"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;4&lt;span&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font color="#003399"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[
2 CONC &lt;/span&gt;5&lt;span&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; called &lt;strong&gt;Charles the Hammer&lt;/strong&gt;, was a &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Frankish&lt;/font&gt; military and political leader, who served as &lt;font color="#003399"&
2 CONC gt;Mayor of the Palace&lt;/font&gt; under the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Merovingian&lt;/font&gt; kings and ruled &lt;em&gt;de facto&lt;/em&gt; during an &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;interregnum&lt;/font&gt; (737&amp;ndash;43) at the end of his lif
2 CONC e, using the title &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Duke and Prince of the Franks&lt;/font&gt;. In 739 he was offered the title of &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Consul&lt;/font&gt; by the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Pope&lt;/font&gt;, but he refused.&lt;s
2 CONC up&gt;&lt;font color="#003399"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;6&lt;span&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; He is perhaps best remembered for winning the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Battle of Tours&lt;/font&gt; in 732, in which he defeated a
2 CONC n invading &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Muslim&lt;/font&gt; army and halted northward Islamic expansion in western Europe.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font color="#003399"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;7&lt;span&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
2 CONC &lt;p&gt;A brilliant general&amp;mdash;he lost only one battle in his career (the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Battle of Cologne&lt;/font&gt;)&amp;mdash;he is a founding figure of the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Middle Ages&lt;/font&gt;, often credi
2 CONC ted with a seminal role in the development of &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;feudalism&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;knighthood&lt;/font&gt;, and laying the groundwork for the &lt;font color="#003399"&gt;Carolingian Empire&lt;/font&gt;.
