2 CONC t;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marie Barbe Kittler&lt;/strong&gt;, native of the duchy of Vitembert, daughter of Jean Mathieu Kittler and Marguerite ____.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull;
2 CONC First husband died German Coast - &lt;strong&gt;Andre Viler&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull;Second husband died German Coast - &lt;strong&gt;Valerien Caquau&lt;/strong&gt;, native of Monterau, diocese of Sens in B
2 CONC urgundy, son of Valerien Caquan and Magdeleine L'Enfant, buried April 10, 1754, in the cemetery of the parish church of the post of the Germans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;bull;Third husband &lt;strong&gt;Gaspard Dubs&lt;/strong&
2 CONC gt;, widower of &lt;strong&gt;Marguerite Hettinger&lt;/strong&gt;, May 24, 1728, recorded in the registers of the parish church of St. Louis of New Orleans, Marriage Book 1, p. 158.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;The birthplace of &lt;strong&gt;Mar
2 CONC ie Barbe Kittler&lt;/strong&gt; was recorded to be Ora in Wurttemberg. &amp;nbsp;In referring to maps of Wurttemberg, no town was found by the name of Ora or Avra; instead, the more likely place of origin was in Bavaria.&amp;nbsp; There exist in th
2 CONC e Schwabeu district of Bavaria two neighboring towns named Aurau and Louisenau.&amp;nbsp; For Catholic registers, both Aurau and Louisenau were filial parishes of Abenberg.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;!--EndFragment--&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></c
2 CONC ontent></metadataxml>
