1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Germain(1) Doucet &lt;br&gt;Dit Sieur de la Verdure&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Dit Laverdure&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;And His Descendants &lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;ul&gt;Germain(1) Doucet came to Acadia i
2 CONC n 1632 with Commader Isaac de Razilly by order of Cardianl Richelieu (Minister of State to King Louis XIII). &lt;br&gt;Germain(1) was a member of THE ORDER OF MALTA.&lt;br&gt;In a document signed July 14, 1640, Germain(1) Doucet was at Port Royal a
2 CONC nd Captain of the Army of Pentagoet as well as the right-hand man (Adjutant) of the Governor of Acadia (Charles de menou d&amp;#39;Aulnay de Charnizay).&lt;br&gt;After the death of the Governor in 1650, Germain(1) was the Commader at the fort of Po
2 CONC rt Royal and Deputy Guardian of the Governor&amp;#39;s children.&lt;br&gt;He returned to France in 1654 with his wife. He left his brother-in-law, Jacques Bourgois, surgeon as Lieutenant of Port Royal.&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pi
2 CONC erre Doucet (My direct Descendant)&lt;/strong&gt;, born 1621 in Sedan, France; died June 02, 1713 in Port Royal, Acadia. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Marguerite Louise Doucet, born Abt 1625 in Port Royal, Acadia; died Aft 1686 in Port Royal, Acadia. &lt;/l
2 CONC i&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Germain(2) Doucet, born 1641 in Port Royal, Married Marguerite Marie Landry in 1664. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;Generation No. 1&amp;nbsp; &lt;hr&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Germain(1) Doucet Dit Sieur de la Verdure(M
2 CONC y direct Descendant)&lt;/strong&gt; was born Abt 1595 in Parish Conflans, Brye(Brie), France (Source: Kristie Kronlage VPKJ53C), and died Aft 1654 in France. He married Marie Bourgeois 1620.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Children of Germain(1) Douce
2 CONC t and Marie Bourgeois are: &lt;br&gt;Children of Germain(1) Doucet from a dispensations grated by the Catholic Church: &lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
