1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;span style="color: black"&gt;Houma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: black"&gt;, LA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style="color: black"&gt;&lt;
2 CONC font size="3"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;: Courier Published: Saturday, August 22, 2009 at 6:01 a.m.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ambert J. Angelette Jr., 86, a native of Golden Meadow and resident of Larose, died Friday, Aug. 21, 2009. Visitatio
2 CONC n will be from 10 a.m. to funeral time today at Falgout Funeral Home of Galliano. Service will be at 1 p.m. today at the funeral home with burial in Sacred Heart Cemetery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He is survived by his wife of more than 64 years, Genevie
2 CONC ve Duet Angelette; one son, Gary A. Angelette and wife, Gwen; one daughter, Donna Lou Angelette Gremillion and husband, Ray; one brother, Steve Angelette; three sisters, Natalie Angelette Toups, Laurina Angelette Eymard and Eloise Angelette Cherami
2 CONC e; six grandchildren; and six great-grandchildren.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was preceded in death by his parents, Ambert Sr. and Nathalie Guidry Angelette; one brother, Roy Angelette Sr.; and one sister, Yvonne Angelette Harvey. He was a member of th
2 CONC e American Legion Post 259 in Golden Meadow and served in WWII in the Army Air Corps as a sergeant in the 371st Fighter Squadron. Falgout Funeral Home of Galliano is in charge of arrangements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font face="Ti
2 CONC mes New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
