2 TITL Baron Philippe Mius Statue
1 _OID 2191ede7-c664-4863-99db-bb73a70a13ff
1 _DSCR Statue of Baron Philippe Mius d'Entremont  Baron Philippe Mius d'Entremont (1601-1699) is the founder of Pobomcoup (today Pubnico) and the forebear of the extended d'Entremont family. The wooden statue was carved by Albert Deveau, a renowned sculpt
2 CONC or from Edmunston, New Brunswick. The statue measures 12 feet high (3.7 m) and was carved from a pine tree 32 inches (90 cm) in diameter using an assortment of saws and chisels. The statue was commissionned by the cultural association of Pubnico, L
2 CONC e Réveil de Pombcoup, who donated it to the Village in August, 1998 during the West Pubnico Acadian Festival. No images of Baron Mius d'Entremont exist; the statue is designed to present a possible likeness of the founder of Pubnico. The sculptor w
2 CONC as also inspired by the painting Sieur Philippe Mius d'Entremont by Père Maurice LeBlanc, c.j.m.
