2 TITL Death of Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr.: How and where and when?
1 _OID 23ba26c2-3152-4f47-807b-9e83641fbf32
1 DATE 1890-92?
1 PLAC Lafourche Parish
1 _DSCR How and when and where did Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr., die?
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The family story&amp;nbsp;was that Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr., was shot by an irate neighbor, a Mr. Cheramie, who believed that he had been insulted by Crosby at a party following a wedding.The sanitize
2 CONC d version of the story (as told by&amp;nbsp;Crosby's youngest daughter Angele)&amp;nbsp;was that&amp;nbsp;Crosby was passing around the wedding cake, and he intentionally skipped Cheramie who,&amp;nbsp;highly insulted, pulled out a gun, and shot Cr
2 CONC osby. Another version of the story&amp;nbsp;is that a jug of whiskey was being passed around, and that Crosby refused to drink after Cheramie. Regardless of which version is accurate, the essential truth is that&amp;nbsp;Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr.,&
2 CONC amp;nbsp;was killed, leaving&amp;nbsp;his wife Emelie with six children to raise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;One of the goals of this research project&amp;nbsp;has been&amp;nbsp;to collect all of the different family versions surround
2 CONC ing&amp;nbsp;Louis Carroll Crosby&amp;rsquo;s death as well as to find a coroner&amp;rsquo;s report, newspaper story, or church record that documents his death. We have many questions about this ancestor as well as about his father Louis Carroll Wa
2 CONC lker Crosby and grandfather Alan/Alen Crosby.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Bernice Bennett, a professional genealogist, has found a newspaper clipping dated June 13, 1891, that says that Louis Croby was killed&amp;nbsp; in Lafourche P
2 CONC arish. The article appears to be&amp;nbsp;from a New Orleans&amp;nbsp;newspaper and is a review of events published in local papers in the preceding months. Chris Hebert, great-great-grandson of Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr., has GEDCOM records that sh
2 CONC ow that Louis was "shot to death by OLucien Cheramie at Pointe Su Sauciese, across from Golden Meadow, LA." Chris also says Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr. made his first communion 24 April 1874 at St. Mary, Raceland, Lafourche, LA. (He would have been 2
2 CONC 3 years old at the time he made his first communion; he married in that church in 1874, and at least some of his and Emelie's children were baptized in that church.)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Until Bernice Bennet foun
2 CONC d the newspaper clipping and Chris backed it up with the information above, we had four dates for the death of Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr.: September of 1890; April of 1891;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;8 November 1892; and 1899. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line>
2 CONC <line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;8 November 1892 is the date Find-A-Grave associated with the grave of a Louis Crosby in the cemetery of Holy Rosary Catholic Church in Larose, LA, However, Jason Griffin, great-grandson of Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr., inter
2 CONC viewed the church secretary who told him&amp;nbsp;that their records show only that&amp;nbsp;a Louis Crosby was buried there in 1899.&amp;nbsp;Angele&amp;nbsp;was born 30 March 1889. In her memoir, &lt;em&gt;Rice on Sunday,&lt;/em&gt; in one plac
2 CONC e she says that her father was killed when she was 18 months old--September of 1890. In another place she says, "My sister Emma married six months after my father died." Emma married in Oct, 1891. Six months earlier would have been April of 1891, t
2 CONC he date that is probably closest to the newspaper account. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;A careful search of the Lafourche newspapers and the records at both the church in Raceland and the court house in Thibodoux shoul
2 CONC d provide the info we're seeking: the circumstances and actual date of Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr., 's death; where he is buried; and whose grave is in the cemetery at Larose!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Angele &lt;span&gt;Crosby Eltz
2 CONC roth Pinckney believed her father&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;was buried in Cut Off; his parents are buried in Griffin Cemetery #2 near Leeville.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
