2 TITL The Melanson Family
1 _OID 23f0a306-caf0-4671-8285-5e45443ebae7
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div align="right"&gt;                  &lt;strong&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The Melanson                    Family&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt
2 CONC ;                    &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;                &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;hr&gt;               &lt;p align="center"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;               &lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;A
2 CONC s                  an Acadian, Nova Scotian and New Brunswickan descendant, I can                  trace my lineage to any number of the main &amp;quot;core&amp;quot; Acadian                  families as can every other Acadian descendant. Most o
2 CONC f these                  &amp;quot;core&amp;quot; families are presented here briefly, beginning                  with the first parents of each of these families to settle in                  Acadia starting in the late 1640&amp;#39;s.&lt;/font&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;/p&gt;               &lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;The                  bulk of my Acadian pages map out my direct Melanson lineage beginning                  with Pierre Laverdure and Priscill
2 CONC a down through their son Charles                  Mellanson dit La Ram&amp;eacute;e and his wife Marie Dugas. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;               &lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;Afte
2 CONC r                  only one actual &amp;#39;Acadian born&amp;#39; generation (Charles &amp;agrave; Charles                  dit La Ram&amp;eacute;e Mellanson &amp;agrave; Pierre Laverdure) my direct-line                  Melanson ancestry then get
2 CONC s caught up in the renaming of Acadia                  into Nova Scotia (around 1713). Although often still referred                  to as Acadia by the French (usually in the French census&amp;#39;) the                  next two generations wer
2 CONC e born in what was now, technically, Nova                  Scotia. These two generations later veer off into northern Nova                  Scotia (to Minudie) for about 30 years due to and after the Deportations                  where a third gene
2 CONC ration was born (Francois &amp;agrave; David Melanson).                  By about 1806 the last of my Acadian-Nova Scotian born ancestors                  (Francois and his father David &amp;agrave; Pierre dit Parrotte Melanson)                  se
2 CONC ttled in southeastern New Brunswick where all subsequent generations                  of my direct-line Melanson ancestors were born.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;               &lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&g
2 CONC t;If                  you have any questions or comments please feel free to email me                  anytime.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;               &lt;div align="center"&gt;                  &lt;strong&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-ser
2 CONC if"&gt;1st Generation&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;                 &lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"&gt; &lt;font size="2" color="#666666"&gt;(for                  each generation page, click on &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;C
2 CONC hildren&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;                  to follow to the next generation page)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt; &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;1
2 CONC .                  &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pierre Laverdure:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt; b. abt 1600-1605, France; d. abt                  1677 (SW).&lt;br&gt;                 &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;font color="#990000"&gt;Married:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;
2 CONC /strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt; abt 1630,                  England (SW), to &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Priscilla --------------&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;                  b. abt 1610 (MCM), England; d. abt 1691, Boston (SW/MCM), Mass
2 CONC .,                  New England. &lt;/font&gt;                &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt; &lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Children:&lt;/u&gt;                  Pierre dit La Verdure Mellanson, Charles dit La Ra
2 CONC m&amp;eacute;e Mellanson                  and John (Laverdure). &lt;/font&gt;                &lt;/p&gt; &lt;font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;font color="#990000"&gt;Priscilla                  Married 2
2 CONC nd&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;font color="#990000"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;                  April 8, 1680, at Boston/Dorchester (SW/MCM), Mass., New England,&lt;font color="#666666"&gt;                  &lt;/fon
2 CONC t&gt;to &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Captain William Wright, Sr.:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;(widow                  of Milah Snow - MCM).&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
