1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>born &amp;amp; baptized Grand-Pr&amp;eacute;, 22 __ 1743; son of Jean-Baptiste MELAN&amp;Ccedil;ON &amp;amp;  Madeleine LEBLANC; brother of Jean-Baptiste, Marie-Rose, Osite, &amp;amp; Paul;  exiled to MD 1755, age 12; ar
2 CONC rived LA 1766, age 23; &lt;u&gt;married&lt;/u&gt;, age 25,  F&amp;eacute;licit&amp;eacute; &lt;span style="background-color: #ffff00"&gt;LANDRY&lt;/span&gt;, daughter of Ren&amp;eacute;  LANDRY &amp;amp; his first wife Marie TH&amp;Eacute;RIOT, 7 F
2 CONC eb 1768, Cabanoc&amp;eacute;; in Cabanoc&amp;eacute;  census, 1769, occupying lot number 142, left [east] bank, age 26, with wife  F&amp;eacute;licit&amp;eacute; age 19, &amp;amp; [widowed] mother Magdelaine LEBLANC age 52; in Ascension  census, 17
2 CONC 70, left [east] bank, age 27, head of family number 57, with wife  F&amp;eacute;licit&amp;eacute; age 20, son Joseph age 8 mos., &amp;amp; 6 arpents; in Ascension census,  1777, left [east] bank, called Charles MELECON, age 32, head of family numbe
2 CONC r  60, with wife F&amp;eacute;licitez age 23, son Alin age 2, daughter Marie age 4, his mother  Magdelaine LEBLANC widow MELENCON age 64, private tutor Claude PEZEE age 50, 11  arpents, 0 slaves, 28 cattle, 2 horses, 0 sheep, 15 hogs, 1 arm; in JUD
2 CONC ICE&amp;#39;s  Company, Acadian Coast Militia, Aug 1779, called Charles MELENCON, fusileer;  died [buried] Ascension 4 May 1787, age 44</line></content></metadataxml>
