1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;ID:&lt;/em&gt;I04786&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Name:&lt;/em&gt; George Dodson &lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; &lt;su
2 CONC p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sex:&lt;/em&gt;M&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Birth:&lt;/em&gt;31 OCT 1737 in Richmond, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><l
2 CONC ine>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Title:&lt;/em&gt;Capt.&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Death:&lt;/em&gt;1825 in Pittsylvania, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note:&lt;/em&gt;</line><line>&lt;blockquote&gt;There is some q
2 CONC uestion that the George whose records follow isactually a son of George and Margaret Dagord Dodson. We have beenunable to locate George and Margaret in records beyond 1756. Until arecord of them can be found after that date, it is not possible togi
2 CONC ve factual information on all their children. The information wehave on their children comes from the North Farnham Parish Registerand the manuscript of Rev. Elias Dodson. Rev. Elias did not name theGeorge under discussion as one of their children
2 CONC . In faxt, he does notrefer to this family at all. Rev. Elias does refer to two Georges aspreachers - "George the Preacher son of Greenham" and "Lame George thePreacher", son of Thomas and Elizabeth Rose Dodson. It may be thatRev. Elias was just a
2 CONC s confused over George as we are an made amistake. Whatever the situation, since descendants have always giventhe family of George Dodson of Pittsylvania, Henry and PatrickCounties in this space on the family tree, we will leave him therewhile caut
2 CONC ioning that there is no proof. Some method of substantiationshould be found.&lt;br&gt;This particular George Dodson was on tax lists of Pittsylvania Co., VAfrom 1782 through 1784 and in Hentry Co. in 1785 through 1790. In 1791Patrick Co. was create
2 CONC d from Henry and his land fell into the newcounty. He was on Patrick Co. tax lists from 1791 through 1796,usually designated as "George Dodson, Sr". In 1797 he returned toPittsylvania Co. where he remained until his death in 1825.&lt;br&gt;It is ve
2 CONC ry difficult to sort him out from other George Dodson in theland records of Pittsylvania Co. In Henry and Patrick Co.'s he isdistinctive. There are many land records there involving him and hissons and their land on Mayo River.&lt;br&gt;There seem
2 CONC s no question of the fact that he was a preacher. THE ANNUALREGISTER OF THE BAPTIST DENOMINATION lists George Dodson as pastor ofSoapstone Creek Church, serving Stokes Co., NC and Henry Co., VA,prior to Nov 1790. George Dodson was "ordained" a Bapt
2 CONC ist minister inPatrict Co., VA on 12 March 1792. It is not certain if both thesereferences are to the same man. A third George Dodson is also in therecords of Pittsylvania, Henry and Patrick Counties who might be thepastor of Soapstone Church.&lt;b
2 CONC r&gt;There is also a question over the names and number of wives of GeorgeDodson. One George Dodson had a wife Margaret in land transactions1777, 1780 and 1783, Pittsylvania Co. We know that the George Dodsonof this sketch had a wife, Elizabeth R
2 CONC . [surname unknow] in 1801 whenthey gave consent for their daughter's marriage to Thomas Chaney. Thewidow of George Dodson, named in his will written in 1816 and probatedin 1825, was Margaret Dodson. It is not possible to tell exactly whichchildre
2 CONC n belonged to which wife. This is a problem of too manyquestions and too little proof. Descendants of this family should tryto resolve some of the conflict by additional research.&lt;br&gt;The children of George Dodson, in order named in his will
2 CONC , were:&lt;br&gt;Thomas Dodson *&lt;br&gt;Jesse Dodson *&lt;br&gt;Leonard Dodson *&lt;br&gt;George Dodson *&lt;br&gt;John Dodson *&lt;br&gt;Robert Dodson *&lt;br&gt;Jethro Dodson&lt;br&gt;Joseph Dodson *&lt;br&gt;Frances Dodson (Spencer) *&lt;br&gt
2 CONC ;Ann Dodson (Shelton)&lt;br&gt;Elizabeth R. Dodson (Chaney)&lt;br&gt;Miriam Dodson (Richardson)&lt;br&gt;Mary Dodson (Madding)&lt;br&gt;Margaret Dodson (Collie or Colley)&lt;br&gt;Rhoda Dodson (Collie or Colley) (2)&lt;/blockquote&gt;</line><line>&
2 CONC lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;em&gt;Father:&lt;/em&gt; George Dodson b: 31 OCT 1702 in North Farnham Parish, Richmond County, Virginia &lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mother:&lt;/em&gt; Margaret Dagord b: 30 APR 1708 in Richmond, Virginia, USA&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em
2 CONC &gt;Marriage&lt;/em&gt; 1 Elizabeth R. LNUChildren&lt;ol&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Thomas Dodsonb: 1765 in Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Jesse Dodsonb: 16 NOV 1772 in Pittsylvania, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt
2 CONC ; Leonard Dodsonb: BET 1767 AND 1774 in Pittsylvania, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; George Dodsonb: 1773 in Pittsylvania, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; John Dodsonb: in Pittsylvania, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</lin
2 CONC e><line>&lt;li&gt; Robert Dodsonb: 1790&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Jethro Dodsonb: 1795 in Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Joseph Dodsonb: in Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Frances Dodsonb: 1792 in Pittsylvan
2 CONC ia, Virginia, USA&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Ann Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Elizabeth R. Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Miriam Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Mary Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Mar
2 CONC garet Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt; Rhoda Dodson&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sources:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;ol&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;Title: http://users.adelphia.net/~rdotson&lt;br&gt;Note: &lt;br&gt;Source Medium
2 CONC : Internet&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;Details: Details: &#x1; Citation Text: Pg 48-50&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;</line><line>&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
