2 CONC earch.com, a web site provided by the Church          of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.&amp;nbsp; There are many different versions,          provided by different researchers.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Another web site entitled &lt;em&gt;th
2 CONC e          Paternal Ancestral Line of Ezekial Springer to Adam and Eve&lt;/em&gt;, by Michael          S. Cole, M. D., contains similar information.&amp;nbsp; Dr. Cole posts the following          ceveat: &amp;ldquo;Note:&amp;nbsp; This lineage i
2 CONC s not adequately documented to fully accept          as accurate.&amp;nbsp; It is intended for enjoyment only and not to be understood          as historically correct.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Keep in mind that &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt
2 CONC ;          such genealogies back to Adam&amp;nbsp;and Eve are suspect.&amp;nbsp; It is my opinion that          the concept of &amp;lsquo;Divine Right of Kings&amp;rsquo; once influenced European rulers          to find a family connection to a wor
2 CONC thy character in the Bible in order          to add validity to their claim to the throne.&amp;nbsp; If the monarch&amp;rsquo;s hired          historian was under threat of execution should he fail to determine the          proper lineage, there i
2 CONC s reasonable expectation that he would be tempted          to fabricate some of the king/queen&amp;rsquo;s ancestry.&amp;nbsp; Don&amp;rsquo;t you agree?&amp;rdquo; &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adam&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Eve&l
2 CONC t;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;were          the first man and woman.&amp;nbsp; One of their sons was &lt;strong&gt;Seth&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seth&lt;/strong&gt; was the          father of &lt;strong&gt;Enos.&lt;/strong&gt
