2 CONC , King of Britain (Old King          Cole, ca. 125, built Coel-Castra, or Colchester) and a daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Cyllin&lt;/strong&gt;,          King of Siluria.&amp;nbsp; Among the children of &lt;strong&gt;Marcomir&lt;/strong&gt; an
2 CONC d          &lt;strong&gt;Athildis&lt;/strong&gt; was &lt;strong&gt;Clodomir IV&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&amp;nbsp;          &lt;strong&gt;Marcomir&lt;/strong&gt; died in 149.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Athildis&lt;/strong&gt; died          in 17
2 CONC 0.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;[&lt;strong&gt;Coilus&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          the son of &lt;strong&gt;Marius.&amp;nbsp; Marius&amp;rsquo;&lt;/strong&gt; father was &lt;strong&gt;Arviragus&lt;/strong&gt;,          and his mother was &lt;st
2 CONC rong&gt;Venissa Julia.&amp;nbsp; Venissa Julia&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          a daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Tiberius Claudius Caesar&lt;/strong&gt;, Emperor of Rome.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;          Tiberius Claudius Caesar&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/stro
2 CONC ng&gt; mother was &lt;strong&gt;Antonia&lt;/strong&gt;,          daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Mark Anthony&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; On his mother&amp;rsquo;s side, &lt;strong&gt;Coilus&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          the grandson of &lt;strong&g
2 CONC t;Boadicea&lt;/strong&gt;, or, in Latin, Victoria, British          queen who poisoned hereself in 62 A.D. after being defeated in battle          by the Romans.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Boadicea&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; husband was &lt;
2 CONC strong&gt;Prasutagus&lt;/strong&gt;.]&amp;nbsp;        &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clodomir IV&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Franks who was born before 149.&amp;nbsp; He married &lt;strong&gt;Hafilda&lt;/strong&gt;
2 CONC ,          and they were the parents of &lt;strong&gt;Farabert&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&amp;nbsp;          &lt;strong&gt;Clodomir&lt;/strong&gt; died in 166.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Farabert&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;wa
2 CONC s          King of Franks who was born before 166 and died in 186.&amp;nbsp; He was father          of &lt;strong&gt;Sunno&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunno&lt;/strong&gt;, or Huano,          was King of F
2 CONC ranks who was born before 186 and died in 213(?).&amp;nbsp; He was          father of &lt;strong&gt;Hilderic&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hilderic&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Franks who wa
2 CONC s born before 212 and died in 253.&amp;nbsp; He was father          of &lt;strong&gt;Bartherus&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bartherus&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Franks who was born befor
2 CONC e 253 and died in 272.&amp;nbsp; He was father          of &lt;strong&gt;Clodius III&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clodius III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Franks who was born before 272 an
2 CONC d died in 289 or 298.&amp;nbsp; He was          father of &lt;strong&gt;Walter&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Walter&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Franks who died in 306.&amp;nbsp; He was fathe
2 CONC r of &lt;strong&gt;Dagobert&lt;/strong&gt;,          King of East Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dagobert&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of East Franks who was born in 230 and died in 317.&amp;nbsp; He was fathe
2 CONC r          of &lt;strong&gt;Genebald,&lt;/strong&gt; Duke of East Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genebald&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;was          Duke of East Franks who was born about 262 and died in 358.&amp;nbsp; He was fathe
2 CONC r          of &lt;strong&gt;Dagobert&lt;/strong&gt;, Duke of East Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dagobert&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          Duke of East Franks who was born about 300 and died in 379.&amp;nbsp; He was fathe
2 CONC r          of &lt;strong&gt;Clodius&lt;/strong&gt;, Duke of East Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clodius&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;was          Duke of East Franks who was born about 324 and died in 389.&amp;nbsp; He was fathe
2 CONC r          of &lt;strong&gt;Marcomir&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marcomir&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          Duke of East Franks who was born about 347 died in 404.&amp;nbsp; He was father          of &lt;strong&gt;Phar
2 CONC amond&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pharamond&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          King of Westphalia, and is considered the first king of the Salian Franks          after the departure of the Romans from Gaul.&amp;nbsp; H
2 CONC e was born about 370, and          he married &lt;strong&gt;Argotta&lt;/strong&gt;, daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Genebald&lt;/strong&gt;,          Duke of East Franks. They were the parents of &lt;strong&gt;Clodius &amp;ldquo;Long Hair&amp;rdquo;,&lt;
2 CONC /strong&gt;          King of the Franks.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clodius&amp;nbsp;&amp;ldquo;Long Hair&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt;,          King of the Franks, was born in 395 in Westphalia.&amp;nbsp; He captured the town          o
2 CONC f Cambrai from the Romans.&amp;nbsp; He married &lt;strong&gt;Basina&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and &lt;strong&gt;Adelbert&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was          their son.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Clodius&lt;/strong&gt; died in 447.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;
2 CONC p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adelbert&lt;/strong&gt; died          in 491.&amp;nbsp; He was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Wambert&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wambert&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;was          born in 480.&amp;nb
2 CONC sp; He the was father of &lt;strong&gt;Ausbert&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ausbert of Moselle&lt;/strong&gt;          was born about 527 in Austrasia on the Schelde, a river which passes through          Antwerp. About 55
2 CONC 6, he married &lt;strong&gt;Princess Blithildus of Sessions&lt;/strong&gt;          (born about 541 in Paris), daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Clothaire I,&lt;/strong&gt; King          of Franks, and &lt;strong&gt;Princess Radegonda of Thuringia. Ausbert
2 CONC &lt;/strong&gt;          and &lt;strong&gt;Princess Radegonda&lt;/strong&gt; were parents of &lt;strong&gt;Arnoldus          (or Arnoul), Bishop of Metz. Ausbert&lt;/strong&gt; died in 570.&lt;br&gt;         &lt;br&gt;         &lt;strong&gt;Arnoldu
2 CONC s (or Arnoul)&lt;/strong&gt; was Bishop of Metz. He was born          about 552 in Austrasia, and married &lt;strong&gt;Dode of Heristal.&lt;/strong&gt;          Among their children may have been &lt;strong&gt;Saint Arnulf (or Arnoul, o
2 CONC r          Arnoldus)&lt;/strong&gt; The elder&lt;strong&gt; Arnoldus&lt;/strong&gt; died in 601.&lt;br&gt;         &lt;br&gt;         Truthfully, nobody knows for sure who the parents of &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf &lt;/strong&gt;were.          Some say t
2 CONC hey were &lt;strong&gt;Arnoldus and Dode&lt;/strong&gt; as stated above.          Others say they were &lt;strong&gt;Bodogisel and Chrodoare&lt;/strong&gt; as described          in Chapter 24.&lt;br&gt;         &lt;br&gt;         &lt;strong&gt;Sain
2 CONC t Arnulf (or Arnoul)&lt;/strong&gt;, Bishop of Metz, son of &lt;strong&gt;Arnoldus          and Dode of Heristal&lt;/strong&gt;, was born August 13, 582. He was a courtier          in the service of Theodebert II of Austrasia. He married &lt;strong
2 CONC &gt;Oda (or          Dode) de Savoy&lt;/strong&gt; , daughter of &lt;strong&gt;Arnoald&lt;/strong&gt;, and they          had two sons, Clodulf and &lt;strong&gt;Ansegisel&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Oda&lt;/strong&gt;          became a nun at Tre
2 CONC ves in 610, and &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf&lt;/strong&gt; dreamed of          becoming a monk at Lerins. However, about 611, &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf &lt;/strong&gt;was          consecrated Bishop of Metz. About 626 &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf&lt;/strong&gt; becam
2 CONC e weary          of his duties, resigned his position, and became a hermit in a solitary          place in the mountains with his friend Romaricus. &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf &lt;/strong&gt;died          August 16, 640 or 641, and was buried by Romaricus
2 CONC . About a year later,          Bishop Goeric transferred his remains to the Basilica of the Holy Apostles          in Metz, Germany. July 18 is the Feast Day of &lt;strong&gt;St. Arnulf&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;         &lt;br&gt;         &lt;stron
2 CONC g&gt;Arnulf&amp;rsquo;s &lt;/strong&gt;son Clodulf later became Bishop of Metz.&lt;br&gt;         &lt;br&gt;         &lt;strong&gt;Ansegisel&lt;/strong&gt;, son of &lt;strong&gt;Arnulf &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;Oda          de Savoy&lt;/stro
2 CONC ng&gt;, was born in 610. He married &lt;strong&gt;Begga&lt;/strong&gt;,daughter          of &lt;strong&gt;Pepin of Landen&lt;/strong&gt; and his wife &lt;strong&gt;Ida&lt;/strong&gt;,          in 635, and &lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;rsquo;Heristal I
2 CONC I &lt;/strong&gt;was among their          children. &lt;strong&gt;Ansegisel &lt;/strong&gt;was murdered in 679 or 685, and &lt;strong&gt;Begga&lt;/strong&gt;          died in 693.&lt;br&gt;       &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;
2 CONC rsquo;Heristal II&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;the          Fat&amp;rdquo;, &lt;/strong&gt;son of&lt;strong&gt; Ansegisel &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;Begga.&lt;/strong&gt; was born in 635.&amp;nbsp;          He inherited im
2 CONC mense landholdings from his parents and was Mayor of the          Palace.&amp;nbsp; He married first Alpaida.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Alpaida died in 705.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;rsquo;Heristal&lt;/strong&gt;          then married Plecturd
2 CONC . &lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;rsquo;Heristal II &lt;/strong&gt;also had a concubine          named&lt;strong&gt; Chalpaida.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;rsquo;Heristal II&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;died December 16
2 CONC ,          714.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charles Martel, &lt;/strong&gt;son of          &lt;strong&gt;Pepin d&amp;rsquo;Heristal II&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Chalpaida,&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/stro
2 CONC ng&gt;was born in 688.&amp;nbsp;          After the death of his father, Plecturd&amp;nbsp;imprisoned him, but he escaped          in 715 and was proclaimed Mayor of the Palace by the Austrasians.&amp;nbsp; A war          between the Austrasians an
2 CONC d the Frankish Kingdom of Neustria followed,          and at the end of the war, &lt;strong&gt;Charles Martel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;was undisputed          ruler of all the Franks.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Charles Mart
2 CONC el&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; greatest achievements          were his defeats of the Muslims from Spain, who invaded France in 732 and again in 739. &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charles Martel&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;married          fir
2 CONC st &lt;strong&gt;Rotrude de Treves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;who died in 724.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Pepin III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(or          Pepin the Short) and Carolman&amp;nbsp;were their sons. He married sec
2 CONC ond Sunnichild,          and he died on October 22, 741, at Quierzy on the Oise River.&amp;nbsp; After his          death, the kingdom was divided between his two sons, Carolman and &lt;strong&gt;Pepin          the Short&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pepin III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(or Pepin the          Short), son of &lt;strong&gt;Charles Martel&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and &lt;strong&gt;Rotrude de Treves,&lt;/strong&gt; was          born in 714 or 715.&amp;nbs
2 CONC p; In 743 he married Bertrada II&amp;nbsp;of Laon (died 783),          and later he married &lt;strong&gt;Gersvind&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; In 751, &lt;strong&gt;Pepin III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;deposed          Childeric III&amp;nbsp;and becam
2 CONC e the first king of the Merovingian Dynasty.&amp;nbsp; Pope          Stephen II&amp;nbsp;crowned &lt;strong&gt;Pepin III&lt;/strong&gt; in 754, and &lt;strong&gt;Pepin&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; army protected          the Pope from the Lombards.&a
2 CONC mp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Pepin&lt;/strong&gt; donated territory to the Pope,          which became the foundation of the Papal States.&amp;nbsp; Among the children of          &lt;strong&gt;Pepin III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and &lt;strong&gt;Gersvind
2 CONC &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was &lt;strong&gt;Charlemagne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; Pepin          III&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;died on September 18, 768, and was buried in the Basilica of St.          Dennis.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt
2 CONC ;strong&gt;Charlemagne, King of &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;France&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charlemagne, &lt;/strong&gt;son of&lt;strong&gt;          Pepin III &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;Gersvind,&lt;/strong&gt;&
2 CONC amp;nbsp;was born April 2, 742, in Ingolheim.&amp;nbsp;          He became King of the Franks in 768, and Emperor of the Romans in 800.&amp;nbsp;          He built a kingdom that included almost all of Western and Central Europe          through mi
2 CONC litary action against the Saxons, Lombards, and Moors, and through          alliances with the Pope.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Charlemagne&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;instituted administrative,          educational, economic, legal, and cultural reform
2 CONC s in his empire.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;He married first &lt;strong&gt;Hildegard&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(757-782)          in 771 at Aix-La-Chapelle (Aachen), and among their children was &lt;strong&gt;Pepin          I&lt;/strong&gt;
2 CONC , King of Italy &lt;span style="color: red"&gt;(See Chapter 10)&lt;/span&gt;.&amp;nbsp; He married second Fastrada of East          Frank&amp;nbsp;in 783.&amp;nbsp; He married third Liutgard of Alemannic&amp;nbsp;in 794, and fourth          Gersuin
2 CONC da of Saxon.&amp;nbsp; Some say that Charlemagne had five wives &amp;ndash; Himiltrude,          Desiderata, &lt;strong&gt;Hildegarde&lt;/strong&gt;, Fastrada, and Luitgarde.&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Louis I&lt;/strong&gt;,          the Pious, was &
2 CONC lt;strong&gt;Charlemagne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; heir. &lt;strong&gt;Charlemagne&lt;/strong&gt; died          on January 28, 814, in Aachen.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Children of Charlemagne were:        &lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;       &lt;p&gt;Pepin the Hunchback&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Louis I&lt;/strong&gt;, the Pious&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Charles, King of Neustria&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Pepin, King of Italy&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Lothar&lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;       &lt;p&gt;five daughters&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;NOTE:&amp;nbsp; In another place, Familysearch.com          says that Pharamond, above, was father of Clodio&amp;nbsp;of Westphalia.&amp;nbsp; Clodio          was fathe
2 CONC r of Merovich, who died in France in 458.&amp;nbsp; Merovich was the father of Cloderic, who died in          Tournai, France, in 481.&amp;nbsp; Cloderic was the father of Clovis the Riparian,          who died in Paris, France, in 511.&amp;nbsp; C
2 CONC lovis the Riparian was father of Childebert, who          died in Cologne, Germany.&amp;nbsp; Childebert was father of Sigebert the Lame , who died in          Cologne in 509.&amp;nbsp; Sigebert the Lame was father of Clodereic the Parricide
2 CONC ,          who also died in Cologne in 509.&amp;nbsp; Cloderic the Parricide was father of          Munderic, who also died in 509.&amp;nbsp; Munderic was the father of Mummolin.&amp;nbsp;          Mummolin was the father of Bodogisel, born befor
2 CONC e 567.&amp;nbsp; Bodogisel was          the father of Arnoul, and Arnoul was the father of Ansegisal.&amp;nbsp; Beginning          with Cloderic, this is the line described &lt;span style="color: red"&gt;in Chapter          24&lt;/span&gt;.&amp;nbs
2 CONC p; So it appears that there is a divergence of opinion about          the lineage from Pharmond to Ansegisal. &lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0pt"&gt;References: 97, 260, 344 &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
