2 CONC h Commander Isaac Razilly (1587-1635) and Charles de Menou d'Aulnay (1604-1650).&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;King Louis XIII of France (1601-1643) responsible for Razilly, a knight in the Order of Malta, the responsibility to repossess the co
2 CONC lony of Acadia English following the Treaty of St-Germain-en- Laye, who returns from Acadia in France.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;Germain Doucet was an officer, a major (Coxswain), among the small group of soldiers who accompanied the missio
2 CONC n.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Razilly left La Rochelle in France July 25, 1632&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Hope in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10
2 CONC pt;"&gt;God,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Berger two transports (hope in God), which was the&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Saint Jehan&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;and landed just three hundred men, three Capuchin Fathers, some varieties of women and children has livestock, seeds, tools, instruments, weapons, ammunition and other supplies to La Have located on the souther
2 CONC n tip of the current Nova Scotia on September 8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;Doucet may have been accompanied on this trip by his son Pierre (1621-1713), my grandfather and his daughter Marguerite Louise (1625-1707), my great-gra
2 CONC ndmother.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 22.53999900817871px; margin: 5pt 0pt 5pt 36pt; text-indent: 36pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Razilly was a cousin of Cardinal Richelieu (15
2 CONC 85-1642) and a member of the Royal Council.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;One of the leaders of the company in New France, he was appointed Lieutenant-General of all parts of New France called "Canada" and the governor of the "Acadia".&lt;/span
2 CONC &gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 24.53999900817871px; margin: 5pt 0pt 5pt 36pt; text-indent: 36pt;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Three months after their ar
2 CONC rival, Razilly Aulnay sent back to Port Royal, which was still occupied by the English.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Doucet, who is always faithful friend Aulnay, accompanied him in this missio
2 CONC n.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;At Port-Royal, the English settlers who wanted to leave the colony and return to England were shipped on the&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10p
2 CONC t; font-style: italic;"&gt;St. Jehan&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;and sent first to LaHave.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Germain Doucet then accompanied the&lt;/sp
