1 _OID 3d90dca6-f5c7-4a15-96e6-9e51edfcfa41
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p style="line-height: 150%" align="left"&gt;Germain Doucet&amp;#39;s older son Pierre was born in France in c1621.&amp;nbsp; He settled at Port-Royal, worked as a mason, and did not marry until c1660, when he was nea
2 CONC rly 40.&amp;nbsp; His wife Henriette, daughter of Simon &lt;strong&gt;Pelletret&lt;/strong&gt;, was 20 years his junior and gave him 10 children.&amp;nbsp; Their four daughters married into the &lt;strong&gt;H&amp;eacute;bert&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;st
2 CONC rong&gt;Bernard&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Doiron&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Ch&amp;ecirc;net Dubreuil&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Comeau&lt;/strong&gt; families.&amp;nbsp; Pierre died at Port-Royal in June 1713; he was 92 years old.&am
2 CONC p;nbsp; Five of his six sons, all born at Port-Royal, created families of their own:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
