1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ansbertus&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Ansbert&lt;/strong&gt;,&a
2 CONC mp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Ausbert&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;was a&amp;nbsp;Frankish&amp;nbsp;Austrasian&amp;nbsp;noble, as well as a&amp;nbsp;Gallo-Roman&amp;nbsp;Senator. He is thought to be the son of&amp;nbsp;Ferreolus, Senator of Narbonne&amp;nbsp;an
2 CONC d his wifeSaint Dode. This would perhaps make him the great-grandson of Sigimerus (son of&amp;nbsp;Clodius) and his wife, a daughter of Ferreolus Tonantius,(a Roman Senator and Praetorian Prefect of Gaul). Therefore, his wife Billihild was daughte
2 CONC r of&amp;nbsp;Charibert I,&amp;nbsp;Merovingian&amp;nbsp;King of Paris, and granddaughter of&amp;nbsp;Chlothar I Magnus.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-
2 CONC size: 13px;"&gt;Little of his actual life is known. Published centuries later&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Liber Historiae Francorum&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;states that an Ansbertus married Blithilde (also called Bilichilde), and that she was the daughter of "Lo
2 CONC thar the father of Dagobert", and then continues the line to the&amp;nbsp;Pippinids&amp;nbsp;through his son&amp;nbsp;Arnoald&amp;nbsp;and his granddaughter&amp;nbsp;Itta&amp;nbsp;(wife of&amp;nbsp;Pepin of Landen).&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;span i
2 CONC d="Chronological_Problems" class="mw-headline"&gt;Chronological Problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mw-editsection" style="-webkit-user-select: none; font-size: small; margin-left: 1em; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 1em; display: inline-b
2 CONC lock;"&gt;[&lt;a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background-image: none; background-position: initial initial; background-repeat: initial initial;" title="Edit section: Chronological Problems" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php
2 CONC ?title=Ansbertus&amp;amp;action=edit&amp;amp;section=1"&gt;edit&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;William of Malmesbury&amp;n
2 CONC bsp;in his&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;History of the Kings of England&lt;/em&gt;, repeats the line, without naming his source.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1em; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[1]&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.
2 CONC 4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;The chronological problems with the line as presented, have led modern genealogists to try to re-construct the line in various ways to fix them.&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;</line><line>&lt;span id="Marriage_and_issue" class="mw-headline"&gt;Marriage and issue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mw-editsection" style="-webkit-user-select: none; font-size: small; margin-left: 1em; vertical-align: baseline; line-height: 1em
2 CONC ; display: inline-block;"&gt;[&lt;a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background-image: none; background-position: initial initial; background-repeat: initial initial;" title="Edit section: Marriage and issue" href="http://en.wikipedia.
2 CONC org/w/index.php?title=Ansbertus&amp;amp;action=edit&amp;amp;section=2"&gt;edit&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;Some moder
2 CONC n reconstructions posit that Ansbertus' wife must be, instead of a daughter of Lothar II, a daughter of Lothar I and make her the offspring of his brief relationship withWaldrada, proposing the following offspring:&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ul styl
2 CONC e="line-height: 19.1875px; margin-: 0.3em; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-: 1.6em; padding: 0px; list-style-image: url(data:image/png; base64,ivborw0kggoaaaansuheugaaaauaaaanaqmaaabb8jblaaaablbmvex///8auow5qsojaaaaaxrstlmaqobyzgaaabnjrefucb1jyeabbqw/wl
2 CONC cagqeagpidyt0ivcsaaaaasuvork5cyii=); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0.1em;"&gt;Arnual or Arnoldus or Arnoald,&amp;nbsp;Bishop of Metz&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;Margrave of Schelde&lt;/li&gt;</lin
2 CONC e><line>&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0.1em;"&gt;Saint Munderic,&amp;nbsp;Bishop of Arisitum&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0.1em;"&gt;Tarsicius or Tarsice&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0.1em;"&gt;Erchinoal
2 CONC d, mayor of the palace of&amp;nbsp;Neustria&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; line-height: 19.1875px; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 13px;"&gt;However the contemporary source&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&lt;em&gt;The History of the Franks,&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;Gregory of Tours, our main source on the&amp;nbsp;Merovingians&amp;nbsp;during the time of this supposed union, does not ascribe to Waldrada any children by her brief unmarri
2 CONC ed relationship with Chlothar.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1em; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[2]&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
