1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font size="5" color="#cccccc"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE SETTLEMENT OF POBOMCOU [Pubnico]&lt;br&gt;  NEAR THE ISLAND OF TOUSQUET&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;  &lt;blockquote&gt; &lt;font size="5" color=
2 CONC "#cccccc"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phillippe MIUS, squire, Sieur de Landremont, 62,  his wife Madelein H&amp;Eacute;LIE; their daughter is Marguerite married to Piere Melanson; their son is 17, other children: Abraham 13,   the younger Phillippe 11, the yo
2 CONC unger daughter Madeleine is 2;  cattle 26; sheep 29, goats 12, hogs 20.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;font size="5"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;This census is translation fro
2 CONC m the extracted study from &lt;em&gt;Les origines fran&amp;ccedil;aises des premi&amp;egrave;res familles acadiennes&lt;/em&gt; by  Nicole T. Bujold and Maurice Caillebeau and edited by the &lt;em&gt;Conseil G&amp;eacute;n&amp;eacute;ral of Vienn
2 CONC a in 1979.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;  The original manuscript, produced by Genevi&amp;egrave;ve Massignon in her thesis &lt;em&gt;Les Parlers Fran&amp;ccedil;ais d&amp;#39;Acadie&lt;/em&gt; is on file at the National Archives of Paris.&lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/blockquote&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
