2 TITL From Adam, the First Man, to Arnoul, Bishop of Metz
1 _OID 48be7bfa-125a-410a-a14a-82b4f5650c7e
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ancestry of Charlemagne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;From Adam, the First Man, to Arnoul, Bishop of Metz &lt;p&gt;The following information is taken primarily from Familysearch.com, a web sit
2 CONC e provided by the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints. There are many different versions, provided by different researchers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another web site entitled &lt;em&gt;the Paternal Ancestral Line of Ezekial Springer to Adam and E
2 CONC ve&lt;/em&gt;, by Michael S. Cole, M. D., contains similar information. Dr. Cole posts the following ceveat: &amp;ldquo;Note: This lineage is not adequately documented to fully accept as accurate. It is intended for enjoyment only and not to be und
2 CONC erstood as historically correct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Keep in mind that &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; such genealogies back to Adam and Eve are suspect. It is my opinion that the concept of &amp;lsquo;Divine Right of Kings&amp;rsquo; once influe
2 CONC nced European rulers to find a family connection to a worthy character in the Bible in order to add validity to their claim to the throne. If the monarch&amp;rsquo;s hired historian was under threat of execution should he fail to determine the prop
2 CONC er lineage, there is reasonable expectation that he would be tempted to fabricate some of the king/queen&amp;rsquo;s ancestry. Don&amp;rsquo;t you agree?&amp;rdquo; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adam&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Eve&lt;/stro
2 CONC ng&gt; were the first man and woman. One of their sons was &lt;strong&gt;Seth&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seth&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Enos.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enos&lt;/strong&g
2 CONC t; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Cainan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cainan&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Mahalaheel&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mahalaheel&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &
2 CONC lt;strong&gt;Jared.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jared&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Enoch&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enoch&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Methusalah&lt;/strong
2 CONC &gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Methusalah&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Lamech.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lamech&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Noah&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;
2 CONC strong&gt;Noah&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: red"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; builder of the ark, was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Shem&lt;/strong&gt;, Ham, and Japheth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shem&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&g
2 CONC t;Arphaxad&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Arphaxad&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Salah&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salah&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Eber.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eber&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Peleg&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peleg&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Reu&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reu&lt;/st
2 CONC rong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Serug&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serug&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Nahor&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nahor&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;str
2 CONC ong&gt;Terah&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Terah&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Abraham&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abraham&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Isaac&lt;/strong&gt;.&l
2 CONC t;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Isaac&lt;/strong&gt; married &lt;strong&gt;Rebecca&lt;/strong&gt;, and they were the parents of &lt;strong&gt;Jacob.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jacob&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;
2 CONC Judah&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Judah&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Zarah&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zarah&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Darda Dordames&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;
2 CONC /p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Darda Dordames&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Erichtleonus&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Erichtleonus&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Tros&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&
2 CONC gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tros&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Iiwas&lt;/strong&gt; (or Iius).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Iiwas&lt;/strong&gt; was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Laomedon&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Laome
2 CONC don&lt;/strong&gt; was King of Troy and was the father of &lt;strong&gt;Prian&lt;/strong&gt; of Italy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prian&lt;/strong&gt;, King of Troy ca 1184 B.C., was the father of a son, &lt;strong&gt;Helenus&lt;/strong&gt; an
