1 _OID 4ca79db3-c96f-4c20-9ebf-1f4dbb7e19aa
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Martaiz&amp;eacute;&lt;/strong&gt; is a commune in the Vienne department in the Poitou-Charentes region in western France. It is a small village about 7 miles from Loudon. In the early 17th century
2 CONC , Martaiz&amp;eacute;, along with the nearby village of La Chauss&amp;eacute;e, was one of the seigneuries of Charles de Menou d&amp;#39;Aulnay. Several of the earliest settlers of Acadia including the &lt;strong&gt;Bourgs&lt;/strong&gt;, the Terri
2 CONC ots, and the Savoies are believed to have been recruited by d&amp;#39;Aulnay from their original home in Martaiz&amp;eacute; to colonize New France. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Source: Wikipedia webpage for &lt;strong&gt;Martaiz&amp;eacute;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;/s
2 CONC up&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perrine Bourg&lt;/strong&gt; b ca 1626 married &lt;strong&gt;Simon Pelletret&lt;/strong&gt; (Peltret) in Acadia ca 1640., then married Rene Landry ca 1645, she d. after census 1693. Perrine an
2 CONC d Simon had two children, &lt;strong&gt;Henriette&lt;/strong&gt; b ca 1641 m Pierre Doucet ca 1660 . Henriette died after the 1693 census.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jeanne&lt;/strong&gt; b ca 1643 married Barnabe Martin ca 1666 then Jacques Vanier di
2 CONC t Langvin ca 1687. Jeanne died 10 jan 1706. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Source: Dictionaire Genealogique Des Familles Acadiennes by Stephen White &lt;br&gt;&lt;!--body: end--&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
