2 TITL Baldwin II, Count of Flanders
1 _OID 4fc75927-9138-4c2a-a532-4f7d56a8fb63
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Baldwin II, Count of Flanders&lt;!-- /firstHeading --&gt;&lt;!-- bodyContent --&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;!-- tagline --&gt;&lt;div&gt;From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- /tagline --&gt;&lt;!-- subtitle --&g
2 CONC t;&lt;!-- /subtitle --&gt;&lt;!-- jumpto --&gt;&lt;div&gt;Jump to: navigation, search &lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- /jumpto --&gt;&lt;!-- bodytext --&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Baldwin II&lt;/strong&gt; (c. 865 &amp;ndash; September 10, 918), nicknamed &lt;em
2 CONC &gt;Calvus&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;em&gt;the Bald&lt;/em&gt;) was the second count of Flanders. He was also hereditary abbot of St. Bertin from 892 till his death. He was the son of Baldwin I of Flanders and Judith, a daughter of Charles the Bald. Throug
2 CONC h his mother, Baldwin was a descendant of Charlemagne.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The early years of Baldwin&amp;#39;s rule were marked by a series of devastating Viking raids. Little north of the Somme was untouched. Baldwin recovered, building new fortres
2 CONC ses and improving city walls, and taking over abandoned property, so that in the end he held far more territory, and held it more strongly, than had his father. He also took advantage of the conflicts between Charles the Simple and Odo, Count of Pa
2 CONC ris to take over the Ternois and the Boulonnias.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 884 Baldwin married &amp;AElig;lfthryth (&amp;AElig;lfthryth, Elftrude, Elfrida), a daughter of King Alfred the Great of England. The marriage was motivated by the common Flemish
2 CONC -English opposition to the Vikings, and was the start of an alliance that was a mainstay of Flemish policy for centuries to come.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In 900, he tried to curb the power of Archbishop Fulk of Rheims by assassinating him, but he was exc
2 CONC ommunicated by Pope Benedict IV.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He died at Blandinberg and was succeeded by his eldest son Arnulf I of Flanders. His younger son Adalulf was (the first) count of Boulogne.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Family&lt;/span&gt;&lt;p&gt;He marri
2 CONC ed &amp;AElig;lfthryth, a daughter of Alfred the Great, King of England. They had the following:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Arnulf I of Flanders (c. 890-964), married Adela of Vermandois&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Adalulf (c. 890-933), Count of Boulogne
2 CONC &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ealswid&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ermentrud&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;His fifth child however, was illegitimate.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Albert (d. 977)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sources&lt;/span&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&g
2 CONC t;&lt;em&gt;Annales Blandinienses&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Folcwine. &lt;em&gt;Gesta Abbatum S. Bertini Sithiensium&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
