1 _OID 52023a20-aa1b-4cb6-8e2d-059fdcc79df5
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Priscilla Wright (Cooper) (b. 1613, d. Dec 1691)&lt;br&gt;Priscilla Wright (Cooper)  was born 1613 in Yorkshire, England, and died Dec 1691 in Boston, Massachusetts.  She married Pierre Melancon dit LaVerdure&amp;lt;http
2 CONC ://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/w/h/y/Laura-S-Whyte/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0213.html&amp;gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;  Notes for Priscilla Wright (Cooper):&lt;br&gt;Priscilla was born in Sterling County,  Scotland. Pierre and Priscilla lande
2 CONC d in Acadie in 1657 after arriving from  England with their sons, Pierre, Charles, and John, on the ship The  Satisfaction.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When Acadie was ceded by the English to the French in the  late 1660&amp;#39;s, both Pierre and Priscill
2 CONC a moved to Boston to avoid the Catholic  French gov&amp;#39;t that was about to take control of Acadie.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She married  William Wright on 4/8/1680 in Boston. In his will, Priscilla was named executrix  and she received his house, th
2 CONC e garden plot adjoining all lands, all goods and  chattel, all debts, and all livestock, she to give to the church at Plymouth  &amp;quot;one ewe lamb&amp;quot; and to friend, Mr. Will Brewster of Plymouth elderthat cloth suit  of apparel which wer
2 CONC e given to me by my brother, Fuller. Brother William  Bradford to be overseer of Priscilla handling the will. His will was dated  9/16/1633.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Records show that Priscilla also married a John Cooper. No  children were recorded in th
2 CONC at marriage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;More About Priscilla Wright  (Cooper):&lt;br&gt;Immigration: 1657, Acadie.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Children of Priscilla Wright  (Cooper) and Pierre Melancon dit LaVerdure are:&lt;br&gt;i.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;+Pierre Melan
2 CONC con  (Mallinson)&amp;lt;http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/w/h/y/Laura-S-Whyte/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0197.html&amp;gt;,  b. 1632, Yorkshire, England, d. Aft. 1714, Nova Scotia, Canada.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
