2 TITL 1671 Census Acadia
1 _OID 558a865b-3af6-4908-a85a-af5542b6e676
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;http://www.acadian-cajun.com/1671cens.htm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1671 Acadian Census&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Here is a transcription of th
2 CONC e first Acadian census. If you have been using the transcription from LeBlanc's book, &lt;em&gt;The Acadian Miracle&lt;/em&gt;, you should be aware that there are errors and omissions. This transcription should be more accurate.&lt;/p&gt;</line><li
2 CONC ne>&lt;p&gt;Most of the entries are from Port Royal, though there are a few from other locations: The Habitation of Poboncom near the Island of Touquet, Cap Neigre, and At Rivier aux Rochelois.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;I also have a graphic c
2 CONC opy of the Original 1671 census at this website.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Surnames are linked to the webpage with up to 6 generations of constructed genealogy.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PORT ROYAL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</
