2 TITL Michel Behrenhart and Marie Anne Hess Alsatian exiles to Louisiana German Coast
1 _OID 56d7fbd5-534a-4d99-8061-6b280a001ac4
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;in 1752, Michel Berenhardt and wife, Marie Anne Hess, son and 4 daughters were among a group of Lutherans trying to cross Alsace Lorraine into Germany in order to practice their Lutheran religion.&amp;
2 CONC nbsp; They were arrested along with 22 other families for trying to cross the border. Their sentence was life imprisonment. They were sent to Saarlouis, France and the men were supposed to serve a life sentence. They made an agreement to change t
2 CONC o Catholicism and accept deportation to Louisiana instead of imprisonment and seperation from family members. Many of these Germans arrived on the German Coast of Louisian around Edgard, St John the Baptist Parish, &amp;nbsp;Louisiana on the left b
2 CONC ank of the Mississippi River. The Berenhardt&amp;#39;s&amp;nbsp;left Metz, France 10 June 1753, arrived in Rochefort, France 3 July 1753, and arrived in New Orleans, Louisiana 8 Sept 1753. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Michel Berenhardt was the son of Hans Be
2 CONC renhardt from Schillersdorf. He married in the Lutheran Church at Schillersdorf, 29 Jan 1726 Anne Marie Hess daughter of Hans Hess from Kirrwiller, who was noted as a shepherd on the marriage certificate. Anne Marie Berenhardt was born 18 Jun 1727
2 CONC , bpt on the 20th&amp;nbsp;; Marie Anne was born 11 Mar 1733 and baptized&amp;nbsp; on 12 th; Catharina b 21 Oct 1735 bpt 24th; Anne Margarete b 14 Jan 1738 bpt 16th; Johann Michel Berenhardt b 23 July 1730; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catharina married Eti
2 CONC enne Toups April 1754&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marie Anne Berehardt married 29 Jan 1754 to Mathias Frederich so f Mathias Frederich and Agnes Klein from Wilersheim in Alsace, &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mathias Frederich was a member of the militia on the German C
2 CONC oast noted in militia record of Jan 1770, as being age 40.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marie Anne Hess , wife of Michel Berenhardt died 14 Dec 1754 buried on German&amp;nbsp; Coast near Edgard, Louisiana in St John Baptist Parish.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Michel Be
2 CONC renhardt did not pass away until after 1765, since he had signed documents regarding sale of land on the left bank to move with Etienne Toups son in law on right bank near Vacherie. This was done just in time since there was an uprising on the lef
2 CONC t bank and the new owners of his land were killed and he survived.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note in records that names will have Spanish translation ex. Juan Baptiste which is probably Johann Baptiste or Jean- father Andres an
2 CONC d mother Marguerite Edelmayer spelled incorrectly as Aidelmayer. marries cousin Marguerite Edelmayer 1786.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
