1 _OID 5c85fe5e-da49-4c51-b3ea-325b1076c315
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;font size="2" color="#000000"&gt;The Franks were a group of Germanic tribes that, about the middle of the 3rd century AD, dwelt along the middle and lower Rhine River. The Franks appeared in th
2 CONC e Roman provinces around 253 and soon thereafter established themselves in two principal groups, the Salian and the Ripuarian. The Salian Franks inhabited the territory along the lower stretches of the Rhine, and the Ripuarian Franks lived along th
2 CONC e middle course of the river. The Salians were conquered by the Roman emperor Julian in 358 and became allies of Rome. During the early 5th century, when the Romans retired from the Rhine, the Salians established themselves in most of the territor
2 CONC y north of the Loire River.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
