1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small; color: #000000;"&gt;MELANSON, Charles, came from England and married at Port-Royal Marie Dugas, according to his grandson Jean Melanso
2 CONC n (&lt;em&gt;Doc. in&amp;eacute;d.&lt;/em&gt;, Vol. III, p. 22).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif;"&gt;Originally a H
2 CONC eugenot, Charles, renounced Protestantism and married Marie Dugas in 1664. (Cl&amp;eacute;ment Cormier, &amp;ldquo;MELANSON, CHARLES,&amp;rdquo; in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;em&gt;Dictionary of Canadian Biography&lt;/em&gt;, vol. 1, University of Toronto/Un
2 CONC iversit&amp;eacute; Laval, 2003&amp;ndash;, accessed April 12, 2015, http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/melanson_charles_1E.html) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
