2 CONC -&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;ACADIAN FAMILIES ACTUALLY DISTRIBUTED TO NEW ENGLAND&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;GOVERNME
2 CONC NT OF BOSTON ~ PROVINCE OF MASSACHUSETTS&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;  &lt;hr&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"
2 CONC &gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;Jean-Baptiste BELLIVEAU, s/o Antoine/Marie TERRIOT, m. to Marguerite MELANSON, d/o Jean/Madeleine ST-SEINE (PETITOT dit ST-SEINE). Child
2 CONC ren: Joseph (1741); Charles (1744); David (1746); Pierre (1748); Marguerite (1750); &lt;strong&gt;Jean (1755)&lt;/strong&gt;; Fran&amp;ccedil;ois (1758); Marie-Madeleine (1762); deported to Boston 1755 with family. At Nicolet, Qu&amp;eacute;bec,  C
2 CONC anada 1766. Jean-Baptiste died at St-Gr&amp;eacute;goire de Nicolet, Qu&amp;eacute;bec, Canada 1808.&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;p style="line-height: 150%"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;Charles BELLIVEAU (brother of Jean Baptist Belliveau),&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;s/o Antoine/Marie TERRIOT, m. to Anne DUGAS. Children: Josep
2 CONC h (1733); Marie-Josephe (1735); Madeleine (1737); Charles (1740); Fran&amp;ccedil;ois (1742); Jean-Baptiste (1744); Marguerite (1746); Anne (1750). Deported to Massachusetts 1755, and at Qu&amp;eacute;bec 1767.&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;p style="line-heigh
2 CONC t: 150%"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'courier new'"&gt;Most likely both Jean Baptiste and Charle
2 CONC s and their families arrived in Boston on the Sloop Seaflower that left Pisiquid on October 27, 1755 and arrived in Massachusetts on November 15, 1755 with 206 Acadians aboard.&lt;/span&gt;  </line></content></metadataxml>
