2 CONC up&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;A&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;&lt;em&gt;BRIBAT&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&lt;em&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;J&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&l
2 CONC t;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;&lt;em&gt;OSEPH&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font size="-1"&gt;2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;em&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;C&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&
2 CONC gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;&lt;em&gt;HARLES&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font size="-1"&gt;1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;em&gt;)&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;was born Abt. 1819 in Bord
2 CONC eaux, Gironde, France, and died December 08, 1894 in Lockport, Lafourche Parish, Louisiana. He married C&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;HARLOTTE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;E&lt;/font&g
2 CONC t;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;MELIE (&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;E&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;MELINA)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;F&lt;/
2 CONC font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;ALGOUT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;April 16, 1846 in Thibodeaux, Louisiana. She was born December 02, 1828 in Thibodeaux, Lafourche, Louisiana, and died Jul
2 CONC y 27, 1906 in Lockport, Louisiana.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color="0000C0"&gt;Notes for&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;G&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;USTAVE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp
2 CONC ;nbsp;J&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;OSEPH&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;A&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;BRIBAT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" siz
2 CONC e="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;S&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;R.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Gustave Abribat Sr. came to the USA in 1838 from France. He married Emelina Falgout in 1846, after wh
2 CONC ich he followed merchandising until after the outbreak of the Civil War. Heopened a large general merchandise store in 1852 and is listed as the overseer of a road in Ward 15 in 1853 and on the Lafourche Parish Assessment Roll in 1867. He applied f
2 CONC or a Firebrand on 4/24/1856. He was listed as a witness for citizenship papers for a Jean Edoward Emile Lafontaine on 10/31/1856. He had a plantation on Bayou Lafourche, Lockport, LA- Valentine Field. He joined the Lafourche Creole Guards, with whi
2 CONC ch he remained fourteen months, and then being over 45 years of age and sick, he returned home after being honorably discharged. He was corporal of the 18th La. regiment and was in the battle of Corinth. He was never wounded.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;H
2 CONC e served in the Confederate Army during the Civil War. He enlisted in G Company, Louisiana 18th Infantry Regiment (18th La. Consolidated Infantry Regiment and Yellow Jacket Battalion) commanded by J. Kleber Gourdain (Regiment&amp;#39;s Organizatio
2 CONC n date- 10/5/1861and Muster date-11/14/1863). He enlisted as a Private at the age of 41. He was promoted to First Corporal on 2/11/1862. (Source: Record of Louisiana Confederate Soldiers, published 1984) Another source listed for him: 2nd Corpl. Co
2 CONC . 6; 18th La. Infantry. En. Camp Moore, Tangipahoa Parish, La. 10/5/1861. &amp;quot;Present all Rolls to June 1862. Roll for July &amp;amp; Aug. 1862. Honorably discharged from service on July 6th 1862 at camp near Tupelo, MS&amp;quot; (according t
2 CONC o Military Records of Confederate Soldiers &amp;amp; La. Confederate Commands Volume I, pp. 20-35, compiled in 1920).&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color="0000C0"&gt;More About&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;G&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Ro
2 CONC man" size="2"&gt;USTAVE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;J&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;OSEPH&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;A&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face=
2 CONC "Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;BRIBAT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;S&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="2"&gt;R.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="3"&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Burial: Decembe
