1 _OID 7e2b9abe-542e-4500-940a-bb52603e3a75
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Source: New Orleans Genesis -&amp;quot;Acadians of Belle-Isle-en-Mer ,1635-1767&amp;quot; by Lepre, Jerome Publication: Santa Cruz County Genealogical Society Library vol. XXXV, no. 138 (Apr 1996; pp .112-120, Pierre Mel
2 CONC ancon: The Elusive Acadian, by John K . Harrel Text: Priscilla MALLESON, an Englishwoman, married around 1630 to Pierre LAVERDURE, a French Huguenot who fled to Yorkshire, England; three sons, two became Catholics and Acadians. The family left Engl
2 CONC and during 1657 bound for Boston, MA, in a group under new Acadian Governor Thomas TEMPLE, an Englishman. They moved to Port Royal,&amp;nbsp; Acadia. After the Treaty of Bredain 1667, they returned to English Boston where Pierre died around 1676. P
2 CONC riscilla married 2nd on 8 Apr 1680 to Captain William WRIGHT. She died in Boston around 1691.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;font color="#003399"&gt;1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
