2 TITL Service in War 1812
1 _OID 869e8922-1f86-4011-b758-d3fb09845056
1 DATE 10 Nov 1814
1 PLAC Kentucky
1 _DSCR Military service in the War of 1812 by Thomas Dodson
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Private Thomas Dodson enlisted on 10 Nov 1814 as a substitute for Samuel Huffner at the age of 49 . During the War of 1812 if you were drafted, but were to old to serve or had health problems a substitute could serve i
2 CONC n your place. This appears to be what Thomas did. He served in the Kentucky Detached Militia in the Company of Captain Jonathan Owsley under the command of Lt. Colonel Gabriel Slaughter. It is not known when he was discharged. There is a POW recor
2 CONC d for a Thomas L. Dodson for the War of 1812, I don&amp;#39;t know if it belongs to this Thomas Dodson. It is the only place I have seen a middle initial. </line></content></metadataxml>
