1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>MELANSON FAMILY&lt;p&gt; To begin ,in Stephen White&amp;#39;s SHA, is the following exert translated;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Pierre Laverdure was a french protestant who married in exile in England  to an english girl name
2 CONC d Priscilla. Brought to Acadie with his family in the spring of 1657 by Thomas  Temple,they settled in Boston after the treaty of Breda in 1667.Two of  their sons married acadian girls and remained in Acadie.Charles the  eldest born around 1643 mar
2 CONC ried Marie Dugas daughter of Abraham Dugas  and Marguerite Doucet. Charles Melanson and Marie Dugas had nine daughters and five sons.Two of  their sons Charles and Jean Melanson were the ancestors of the  Melansons of southwest New Brunswick.&lt;br
2 CONC &gt; The nine daughters of Charles and Marie Dugas were:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Marie born around 1664 &lt;br&gt; Marguerite born around 1666&lt;br&gt; Anne born around 1668&lt;br&gt; Cecile born around 1671&lt;br&gt; Elizabeth born around 1673&lt;br&g
2 CONC t; Madeleine born around 1677&lt;br&gt; Marie born around 1680&lt;br&gt; Francoise born around 1683&lt;br&gt; Marguerite born around 1693&lt;br&gt; The five sons were:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Charles born around 1675 married Anne dit Joanne Bourg aroun
2 CONC d 1700.&lt;br&gt; Claude born around 1688 married Marguerite Babineau Jan.22 1714 in Port Royal.&lt;br&gt; Jean born around 1690 married Marie Madeleine Petitot dit Saint Seine in Port Royal Jan.22 1714&lt;br&gt; Pierre born around 1685 married Ann
2 CONC e Granger Nov 7 1712 in Port Royal, Pierre was twin to Ambroise&lt;br&gt; Ambroise born around 1685 married twice first to Francoise Bourg Nov 10  1705 in Port Royal , then to Marguerite Comeau Jan.23 1719 in Port Royal&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;http://www.acadian-roots.com/genealogy-quinan.html &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
