1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;It seems Allen Crosby was involved in another area of Winston County, Mississippi. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Article from Winston county history: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gypsey was the name of a post office located near th
2 CONC e Gumbranch  		Community twelve miles north of Louisville. This site was settled in  		1835 by Allen Neighbors, Ezekiel Barron, William Shaw, Allen Crosby and  		Samuel Hyde. On the establishment of a post office, William Griffith  		served as post
2 CONC master until the office was discontinued in 1902. An early  		school in the community known as Shaw Spring was consolidated with  		Gumbranch in 1925. &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
