1 _DSCR From &quot;Remember Us&quot; - Historical Biographical Pictorial by Lucien and Melba Martin
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="comic sans ms,sand"&gt;Pierre Melancon, born in 1632, was a stone mason by trade.&amp;nbsp; About 1664 he was married in Port Royal to Marie-Marguerite Mius d&amp;#39;Entremont, the dau
2 CONC ghter of Phillippe Mius d&amp;#39;Entremont de Pobomcoup and Madeleine Elie.&amp;nbsp; Pierre, who had been a Calvinist, converted to Catholocism when he married.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="comic sans ms,sand"&gt;Pierre and Margu
2 CONC erite made their home in Port Royal where they are listed in the census of 1671.&amp;nbsp; In 1680 Pierre sold his property in Port Royal and moved his family to Grand Pre to begin a colony.&amp;nbsp; They were the first and only settlers until 168
2 CONC 2 when Pierre Terriot arrived to start another colony on the Saint-Antoine River not far from Pierre Melancon&amp;#39;s settlement.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="comic sans ms,sand"&gt;Pierre and Marguerite are listed in the Bay o
2 CONC f Mines (Grand Pre) census of 1686 which states they had four sons and five daughters.&amp;nbsp; At this time Pierre had 31 head of cattle and an arsenal of 12 guns.&amp;nbsp; Later he was named Major-in-Charge of the Militia and for several year
2 CONC s was in charge of the commercial affairs of Alexandre Le Borgne de Belle Isle.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="comic sans ms,sand"&gt;Children: Philippe, b. 1666; Cecile, b. 1668; Pierre, b. 1670; Marie, b. 1673; Marguerite, b. 1676
2 CONC ; Isabelle, b. 1679; Jean b. 1681; Madeleine, b. 1684; Anne, b. 1686; Paul B. 1691.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
