1 _OID a16a470e-49a1-4110-89c6-6409a3e00009
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;Notes for &lt;strong&gt;Pierre Melancon dit LaVerdure&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;The  name Melancon is also spelled as Melanson.  It&amp;#39;s considered an old  French name however, it reall
2 CONC y is a &amp;quot;Gallicized&amp;quot; version of the English  name, Mellison.In 1657, Pierre and his family left aboard the ship  &amp;quot;Satisfaction&amp;quot; under the command of Capt. Peter Butler.  Pierre and  Priscilla settled in Acadia.  &
2 CONC lt;br&gt;Later on, Pierre&amp;#39;s son, John, was  found guilty of tricking some Indians from near Cape Sable, Acadia, onto  a vessel so they could sell them as slaves on Fayal Island.  17  Indians, men, women, and children were involved.  This wa
2 CONC s illegal, and  they were arrested.  John was granted temporary leave (bail) for 100  pounds supplied by Samuel Sendall, whom his mother referred to as her  landlord.  John never made it to trial and disappeared.  His father,  Pierre, searched fo
2 CONC r him asfar as Acadia but never found him.  The  journey weakened him and he died in 1677.  Priscilla, depended on the  town with charity as she was obligated to repaythe 100 pounds to her  landlord (Samuel Sendall).  Later, she married Captain Wil
2 CONC liam Wright,  an innkeeper from Dorchester, Mass. on 4/8/1680.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;More About &lt;strong&gt;Pierre Melancon dit LaVerdure&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;Immigration: 1657, Left France for Nova Scotia.&lt;br&gt;Religion: ; Religion: Frenc
2 CONC h Huguenot.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Children of &lt;strong&gt;Pierre Melancon dit LaVerdure&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Priscilla Wright (Cooper)&lt;/strong&gt; are:  &lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;+&lt;strong&gt;Pierre Melancon (Mallinson)&lt;/strong&gt;, b
2 CONC . 1632, Yorkshire, England, d. Aft. 1714, Nova Scotia, Canada.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
