1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ALEXANDRIA DAILY TOWN TALK, SATURDAY, MARCH 5, 1988&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOUDELL H. PARKER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Services for Loudell H. Parker will be at 1:3
2 CONC 0 pm Sunday in the chapel of John Kramer &amp;amp; Son.&amp;nbsp; Burial will be in Alexandria Memorial Gardens.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Parker, 80, of Alexandria died Friday in her residence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She was a member&amp;nbsp; of Emmanue
2 CONC l Baptist Church and the Rapides General Hospital Auxilary.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Survivors include two daughters, Cynthia Parker Howell of Lancaster, S.C., and Carol Parker Graham of Alexandria; one sister, Opal L. Morgan of Bertran, Texas; nine grand
2 CONC children and six great-grandchildren.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Friends may call from 4 pm until 6 pm today and from 8 am until time of services in the funeral home Sunday.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
