1 _OID ab3ac9b7-69e9-4d94-b0dd-8e6af8376652
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;New Orleans, Louisiana&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;The Times-Picayune newspaper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;
2 CONC p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Monday, May 14, 1973, Pg. 16&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;DOUCET - Alice Melancon Doucet, at Raceland, La., on Sunday, May 13, 1973, at 11:00 o'clock a.
2 CONC m., wife of the late Firman Doucet Sr.; mother of Mrs. Louis Dantin, Mrs. Russell Dominique, Mrs. Constant Lafant; also Dewey, Norris, Ocean, Freddie and Wesley Doucet; also the late Firman Jr. and Eddie Doucet; sister of Theogene Melancon, Mrs. At
2 CONC enize Lee, Mrs. John Plaisance; also the late Theodore, Andrew and Arthur Melancon Jr., Mrs. Joseph Mobley, Mrs. Celestine Collins, and Mrs. Louise Toups; survived by 27 grandchildren, 55 great grandchildren and 10 great great grandchildren, age 8
2 CONC 4 years, a native of Golden Meadow, La., and a resident of Cut Off, La. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Relatives and friends of the family are invited to attend the funeral.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
2 CONC </line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Services from Falgout Funeral Homes, Inc., Galliano, La., on Tuesday, May 15, 1973 at 9:30 o'clock a.m.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Re
2 CONC ligious services at St. Sacred Heart Catholic Church, Cut Off, La. at 10 a.m.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Interment in church cemetery. Arrangements by Falgout.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></co
2 CONC ntent></metadataxml>
