1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>A letter by Joseph&amp;#39;s father (Francis) states: &amp;quot; Ville de Bordeau, dated 2/28/1819; at eleven in the morning on March 2, 1819, has appeared Mrs. Cazal, wife of Bonnet, 24 years old, a midwife, living nort
2 CONC h the cross street, who has presented to us a child of masculine sex, a son of Francis Abribat, refiner, declaring, and of Marguerite Bouguie, his wife, and to whom he gives the forename of Joseph- done in the presence of P. LaChappelle, a plante
2 CONC r and colonist, St. Louis St. No. 32; Joseph Corne, a retired soldier.&amp;quot;</line></content></metadataxml>
