2 CONC &gt; &lt;p align="center"&gt;For a chronology of Acadian Arrivals in Louisiana, 1764-early 1800s, see Appendix. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p align="center"&gt; The hyperlink attached to an individual&amp;#39;s name is connected to a list of Acadian immigrant
2 CONC s for a particular settlement and provides a different perspective on the refugee&amp;#39;s place in family and community.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;    &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;     &lt;td width="20%" height="21"&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Name&lt;/font&gt;&
2 CONC lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="7%" height="21"&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Arrived&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="6%" height="21"&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Settled&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="69%" height="21"&gt;&lt;font size="4"&g
2 CONC t;Profile&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;/tr&gt;   &lt;tr&gt;     &lt;td width="26%"&gt;&lt;a name="Jacques Mius D'ENTREMONT" href="http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-Acadians%20to%20Lafourche,%201785.htm#Jacques%20Mius%20D%27ENTREMONT,%20fils
2 CONC "&gt;Jacques Mius         &lt;strong&gt;D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT&lt;/strong&gt; IV&lt;/a&gt; &lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;a name="01" href="http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-D%27ENTREMONT.htm#01."&gt;01&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;     &lt
2 CONC ;td width="7%"&gt;Dec 1785&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="7%"&gt;Asp&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="60%"&gt;born c1756, probably Pobomcoup; son of Jacques Mius D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT       III &amp;amp; Marguerite LANDRY; deported Louisbourg to Cherbourg
2 CONC , France,       1758-59, age 2; at Cherbourg, France, 1767, age 11; &lt;u&gt;married&lt;/u&gt; Marie &lt;span style="background-color: #00ffff"&gt;HERVE&lt;/span&gt;       of St.-Brieuc, St.-Malo, France, widow         of Louis LONDROMON &lt;em&gt;
2 CONC dit&lt;/em&gt; LANGLINAIS of St.-Malo, early 1780s, probably St.-Malo; wedding witness       (signed) Feb 1784, St.-Servan,       France; granted a captaincy by the Spanish authorities         because of the nobility of his family &amp;amp; their s
2 CONC ervice as         &amp;quot;governors&amp;quot; in Acadia, Oct 1784;         sailed to LA on &lt;em&gt;La Ville d&amp;#39;Archangel&lt;/em&gt;, age 29, head of  family, no  	occupation listed; in Valenzu&amp;eacute;la census, 1788, left bank
2 CONC ,         called Jacques Mius DENTREMONT, age 30, with no wife so probably  a         widower, daughter Martines age 2, stepson Jean[-Louis] LANGLINAY  age 14,         stepdaughter Ang&amp;eacute;lique LANGLINAY age 10, 1 slave, 8 arpents, 15  qts
2 CONC .  	corn, 1 horned cattle, 1 swine; in Valenzu&amp;eacute;la census, 1791, left bank,  called Jacques Minus DENDREMONT, age 34, with no wife listed,         stepdaughter Marie LANGLIER age 16, Ang&amp;eacute;lique [LANGLIER] age 14,         daughte
2 CONC r Martine age 5, 1 slave, 10 arpents, 0 qts. rice, 60  qts. corn,         1 horned cattle, 0 horses, 10 swine&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;/tr&gt;   &lt;tr&gt;     &lt;td width="26%"&gt;&lt;a name="Jacques-Ferdinand Mius D'ENTREMONT" href="http://www.acadiansi
2 CONC ngray.com/Appendices-Acadians%20to%20Lafourche,%201785.htm#Jacques-Ferdinand%20Mius%20D%27ENTREMONT"&gt;Jacques-Ferdinand Mius D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT&lt;/a&gt;       &lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;a name="02" href="http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-A
2 CONC TLAL-D%27ENTREMONT.htm#02."&gt;02&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="7%"&gt;Dec 1785&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="7%"&gt;Asp?&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="60%"&gt;born c1784, France; son of Jacques Mius D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT IV &amp;
2 CONC amp; Marie       HERVE; brother of Marie/Martine; sailed to LA on &lt;em&gt;La Ville d&amp;#39;Archangel&lt;/em&gt;,         age 1; &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; in Valenzu&amp;eacute;la census of 1788 with the rest of his         family, so he probabl
2 CONC y died young&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;/tr&gt;   &lt;tr&gt;     &lt;td width="26%"&gt;&lt;font size="1"&gt;*&lt;/font&gt;&lt;a name="Marie/Martine Mius D'ENTREMONT" href="http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-Acadians%20to%20Lafourche,%201785.htm#Marie/M
2 CONC artine%20Mius%20D%27ENTREMONT"&gt;Marie-Martine Mius D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT&lt;/a&gt;       &lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;a name="03" href="http://www.acadiansingray.com/Appendices-ATLAL-D%27ENTREMONT.htm#03."&gt;03&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;     &l
2 CONC t;td width="7%"&gt;Dec 1785&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="7%"&gt;Asp, Atk&lt;/td&gt;     &lt;td width="60%"&gt;sailed to LA on &lt;em&gt;La Ville d&amp;#39;Archangel&lt;/em&gt;;         born probably aboard ship; called Martine, daughter of Jacque
2 CONC s         Mius D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT IV &amp;amp; Marie HERVE; sister of         Jacques-Ferdinand; baptized c25 Oct[probably Dec] 1785, New Orleans,  	soon after the family reached LA; in Valenzu&amp;eacute;la census, 1788, left bank, called Martine
2 CONC s,  	age 2, with widowed father &amp;amp; half-siblings; in Valenzu&amp;eacute;la census, 1791,         left bank, called Martine, age 5, with widowed father &amp;amp; 2         half-siblings; moved to Attakapas District; &lt;u&gt;married&lt;/u&gt;
2 CONC , age 17, Jean-Baptiste         &lt;span style="background-color: #ffff00"&gt;TRAHAN&lt;/span&gt;, son of Athanase TRAHAN &amp;amp;         Madeleine THIBODEAUX, 27 Jul 1802, Atakapas, now St. Martinville;       settled at La Grosse &amp;Icirc;le &
2 CONC lt;em&gt;du&lt;/em&gt; Vermilion; died St. Martin Parish, 5:00 p.m., 28 Oct 1807, age       23, buried next day&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;   &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt; &lt;p align="center"&gt;NOTES&lt;/p&gt; &lt;blockquote&gt;   &lt;blockquote&gt;     &l
2 CONC t;p align="left"&gt;01.&amp;nbsp; &lt;em&gt;Wall of Names&lt;/em&gt;,     46, calls him Jacques Mieus D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT; Winzerling, &lt;em&gt;Acadian Odyssey&lt;/em&gt;, 108, 185, note     86, calls him D&amp;#39;ANTREMONT, &amp;amp; says in not
2 CONC e 86 that the Spanish granted him the rank of &amp;quot;captain general &amp;#39;de referida Provincia&amp;#39;.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp; See also     Robichaux&lt;em&gt;, Acadians in St.-Malo&lt;/em&gt;, 1099; Robichaux&lt;em&gt;, Bayou Lafourche
2 CONC ,     1770-98&lt;/em&gt;, 43, 175.&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt; The D&amp;#39;ENTREMONTs were never governors of Acadia but were indeed of a noble family &amp;amp; held the seigneury of Pobomcoup, now Pubnico, near Cap-Sable.&amp;nbsp; D&am
2 CONC p;#39;ENTREMONT&amp;#39;s ancestor also served as the King&amp;#39;s attorney in Port-Royal.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;For the likely scenario of his deportation to France, see     the footnote     for his mother&amp;#
2 CONC 39;s profile.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;Judging from the ages of his stepchildren &amp;amp; from the     ages of his own children by Marie HERVE, Jacques &amp;amp; Marie were married     sometime in the early 1780s, wh
2 CONC en he was in his late 20s.&amp;nbsp; Jacques&amp;#39;s     wife&amp;#39;s first husband&amp;#39;s name is from the May 1796 marriage record of     stepdaughter Marie-Jeanne LANGLINAIS in &lt;em&gt;BRDR&lt;/em&gt;, 2:451 (SJA-2, 34), which calls he
2 CONC r     Maria LANGLINETTE; also in stepson Jean-Louis&amp;#39;s daughter Marie-Perronille&amp;#39;s     1797 baptismal record in H&amp;eacute;bert, D., &lt;em&gt;Southwest LA Records&lt;/em&gt;,     1-A:482 (SM Ch.: v.5, #2), which calls him Louis LA
2 CONC NGLINAIS of St.-Malo     &amp;amp; his father also Louis LANGLINAIS of St.-Malo.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;Evidently Jean-Louis, called Louis, stepson of  Jacques Mius     D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT, was the progenitor of th
2 CONC e French Creole LANGLINAIS  family in     South LA; he married an Acadian girl, C&amp;eacute;leste, daughter of Ren&amp;eacute;  LEBLANC, at     Attakapas, now St. Martinville, in Sep 1794, 9 years after he  reached     LA.&amp;nbsp; See H&amp;eacu
2 CONC te;bert, D., 1-A:482(SM Ch.: v.4, #102).&amp;nbsp; I call the  LANGLINAISs French Creoles because they came to LA before 1803, &amp;amp;,     despite the LANGLINAIS association with the Acadian D&amp;#39;ENTREMONTs,  the     LANGLINAISs never live
2 CONC d in Acadia but were from St.-Malo,  specifically St.-Servan,     a suburb of St.-Malo.&amp;nbsp; (Sorry, Pauline, but I tried.)&amp;nbsp;     LANGLINAIS in fact may have been a &lt;em&gt;dit&lt;/em&gt; name.&amp;nbsp; The burial     record of on
2 CONC e of Jean-Louis&amp;#39;s daughters who died at age 7 days in Dec 1799, &amp;amp;     the baptismal record of another daughter born in Jan 1801, called him Jean LANDROMON &lt;em&gt;dit&lt;/em&gt; LANGLINAIS.&amp;nbsp; See H&amp;eacute;bert, D.
2 CONC ,     1-A:482 (SM Ch.: v.4, #197), 1-B:437.&amp;nbsp; The family&amp;#39;s name also is     spelled LANGLINE, LANGLAIS, LANGLINOIS, &amp;amp; is not to be confused with the     more numerous French Creole LANGLOIS family who also lived in the Attak
2 CONC apas     region.&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;02.&amp;nbsp; &lt;em&gt;Wall of Names&lt;/em&gt;,     46, calls him Jacques-Ferdinand Mieus D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT.&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;p align="left"&gt;Did he survive the crossing from France?&lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;03.&amp;nbsp; Not in &lt;em&gt;Wall of     Names&lt;/em&gt; because of the circumstance of her birth.&amp;nbsp; &lt;em&gt;NOAR&lt;/em&gt;, 4:74     (SLC, B9, 390),     her birth/baptismal record, calls her Maria DE ANTRE
2 CONC MUT, gives her parents&amp;#39;     names, says she was baptized &amp;quot;[* - cir. Oct.] 25, 1785,&amp;quot; does not     give her birth date, &amp;amp; says her godparents were Gilverto     LEONARD &amp;amp; Luisa BROMI[CI?]; Arsenault, &lt;em&g
2 CONC t;G&amp;eacute;n&amp;eacute;alogie&lt;/em&gt;, 2471, calls her     Martine D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT;     H&amp;eacute;bert, D., &lt;em&gt;Southwest LA Records&lt;/em&gt;, 1-B:204-05, 711 (SM Ch.: v.4, #256), her marriage record,     calls her Martine D&
2 CONC amp;#39;ENTREMONT of New Orleans, gives her &amp;amp; her husband&amp;#39;s  	parents&amp;#39; names, spells her father&amp;#39;s surname DANTREMON, gives her mother&amp;#39;s hometown in France,  	says his parents&amp;#39; were &amp;quot;of Acadia
2 CONC ,&amp;quot; &amp;amp; that the witnesses     to her marriage were Carlos FAGOT, Jean LANGLINAIS [her stepbrother], Joseph     TRAHAN, &amp;amp; Pierre TRAHAN; H&amp;eacute;bert, D., &lt;em&gt;Southwest LA Records&lt;/em&gt;,     1-B:204-05 (SM Ch.
2 CONC : v.4, #482), her death/burial record, calls her Martine     D&amp;#39;ENTREMONT, &amp;quot;m. to Jean-Baptiste TRAHAN of &lt;em&gt; La Grosse Ile du Vermillion&lt;/em&gt;,     a native of New Orleans,&amp;quot; gives the exact time of her death, s
2 CONC ays she died     &amp;quot;at age 23 yrs.,&amp;quot; but does not give her parents&amp;#39;     names.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;She was one of the newborn infants named after Martin NAVARRO, the Spanish intendan
2 CONC t     of LA, who stood as honorary godfather to their newborns, hence her name     Martine.&amp;nbsp; See notation in 	 	appendix.&amp;nbsp;     She could not have been baptized at New Orleans in late Oct since her ship     did not reach New Orlean
2 CONC s until early Dec.&amp;nbsp; Perhaps the recording     priest meant to say that she was &lt;em&gt;born&lt;/em&gt; in late Oct.&amp;nbsp; &lt;em&gt;La Ville     d&amp;#39;Archangel&lt;/em&gt; left St.-Malo on 12 Aug 1785 and was at sea for 113 days
2 CONC ,     until 3 Dec.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;     &lt;p align="left"&gt;Considering her age at the time of her death, she probably died from childbirth.&amp;nbsp;     She and her husband had at least 2 children--Ad&amp;eacute;la&amp;iuml;de, bor
2 CONC n in Jun 1804,     and Eus&amp;egrave;be in Aug 1806--before she died.&amp;nbsp; Eus&amp;egrave;be married distant     cousin Marie Emilite, called Melite, daughter of Olivier TRAHAN, in     Lafayette Parish in Jan 1829, so the D&amp;#39;ENTREMON
2 CONC T blood lived on in LA.&amp;nbsp;     See H&amp;eacute;bert, D., &lt;em&gt;Southwest LA Records&lt;/em&gt;, 1-B:706, 709,     2-C:752.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/blockquote&gt; &lt;/blockquote&gt; &lt;p align="center"&gt;[top of page D&am
2 CONC p;#39;ENTREMONT]&lt;/p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Copyright (c) 2007-12&amp;nbsp; Steven A. Cormier&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
