2 CONC dium;"&gt;Margaret Walker married Reverend Samuel Houston in 1795. She was a daughter of Joseph, who was long a ruling elder in the Falling Springs Church. She had a well balanced mind and retentive memory; was very religious. At 83 years of age sh
2 CONC e still retained the manner and appearance of a much younger woman ; was often found ministering to the sick and afflicted of the neighborhood Mary Moore, the captive of Abb's Valley, was brought up with Margaret Walker, being her first cousin. Mar
2 CONC garet Walker Houston died at her home, "Rural Valley," Aug.. 14, 1854, and was buried in the cemetery of "High Bridge Church.'' &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
