1 _OID de4a955a-309c-4292-932f-d633d6008a55
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Grand-Pr&amp;eacute; (French for &lt;em&gt;great meadow&lt;/em&gt;) is located on the shor
2 CONC e of the Minas Basin, an area of tidal marshland, first settled about 1680 by Pierre Melanson dit La Verdure, his wife Marguerite Mius d'Entremont and their five young children who traveled east from Pierre Dugua, Sieur de Mons's original settlemen
2 CONC t at Port-Royal which was the first capital of the French settlement of Acadia (&lt;em&gt;Acadie&lt;/em&gt; in French).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Pierre, an Acadian of French Huguenot and English extraction, had arrived in Port Royal with Sir Thomas Temple in the 1
2 CONC 650s when Acadia was under English control. The fertility of the soils and wealth of other resources in the area had been known to the French since the early part of the century when Samuel de Champlain, de Mont's cartographer, had surveyed the reg
2 CONC ion. The settlers quickly employed their dyke building technology to to hold back the tides in the vast salt marshes of the Minas Basin; effectively reclaiming several thousand acres of productive farm land. The farms and the population grew quickl
2 CONC y, making Grand-Pr&amp;eacute; the principal settlement in Acadia. Settlements spread from Grand-Pr&amp;eacute; around the Minas Basin, collectively becoming known as Les Mines or Minas after the copper deposits surveyed by De Monts at the entranc
2 CONC e to the Basin. By the mid-1680s the population was sufficient to support a church and the parish of Saint-Charles de Mine was formed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: s
2 CONC mall;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial,helvetica,sans
2 CONC -serif;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;From Wikipedia.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
