2 TITL Priscilla Mallanson
1 _OID e7928a5a-a33b-4e8a-aa7d-68b9467cb769
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>The family traveled with the newly appointed Acadian Governor Thomas Temple on the ship Satisfaction from England.&amp;nbsp; Charles, his older bother Pierre, and brother Jean came to Acadia with their parents in 1657.&a
2 CONC mp;nbsp; They were born in Scotland.&amp;nbsp; Charles was 14 years old at the time.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Pierre was French and Priscilla was English.&amp;nbsp; He was a Huguenot who moved to England from France before 1632.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prisc
2 CONC illa&amp;#39;s last name is open to some question.&amp;nbsp; Some authors consider it unkown.&amp;nbsp; Others feel the family name of Melanson comes from her rather then Pierre.&amp;nbsp; Others feel the name is Mallanson.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The f
2 CONC amily likely originally settled on the St. John River. Then in 1667, when Acadia was returned to France by the Treaty of Breda, Pierre and Pricilla moved to Boston with their son Jean.&amp;nbsp; Charles eldest daughter, Marie (born 1664) was raise
2 CONC d by her grandparents in Boston.&amp;nbsp; Charles and Pierre remained in Acadia.&amp;nbsp; We are directly descended from two of their children, Charles and Pierre.&amp;nbsp; The Charles Melanson home site is a historical landmark.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br
2 CONC &gt;Pierre had the dit name of Laverdure.&amp;nbsp; This was also used by his son Jean (John) and his granddaughter Marie (daughter of Charles).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Her son Jean (John Laverdure) was arrested for abducting Native Indians and he disap
2 CONC peared while out on bail.&amp;nbsp; John Laverdure&amp;#39;s disappearance left his parents responsible for repaying the &amp;pound;100 he had borrowed for his bail.&amp;nbsp; Pierre Laverdure Melanson sailed to Acadia in the hope of finding John w
2 CONC ith his brothers, Pierre and Charles Mellanson, and bringing him back to Boston.&amp;nbsp; Pierre Laverdure did not find John in Acadia and died soon after, leaving Priscilla to deal with John&amp;#39;s debt.&amp;nbsp; Priscilla appealed to the Bos
2 CONC ton court to reduce or waive John&amp;#39;s bail, but her petition was refused.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Priscilla remarried in 1680.&amp;nbsp; Her new husband was Capt. William Wright, Sr.&amp;nbsp; Priscilla compiled an inventory of the household good
2 CONC s she brought into her new marriage and she signed it with the initials &amp;quot;PM.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp; Priscilla said that when she died, all of her goods were to go to her granddaughter Mary Laverdure (Marie Melanson).&amp;nbsp; But when Prisci
2 CONC lla died, her second husband refused to give her goods to Mary Laverdure and Mary Laverdure (Marie Melanson) sued Capt. Wright for her grandmother&amp;#39;s goods.</line></content></metadataxml>
