2 TITL Crosby Cemetery, Leeville
1 _OID e85b4339-a18d-4631-b229-710dae295b1b
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;font face="arial,helvetica,sans-serif"&gt;The Crosby Cemetery at Leeville is also known as Griffin Cemetery No. 2, according to Paul Chiquit of the South Lafourche branch of the Lafourch
2 CONC e Public Library. Mr. Chiquit says the &amp;quot;cemetery was established by Isaac George Griffin for his wife Laura Batistile Crosby who was the daughter of Louis Carroll Thomas Crosby [&lt;em&gt;sic&lt;/em&gt;] and Eveline Marie Dantin. Laura Bat
2 CONC istile Crosby wanted a place to bury her father and mother...and other family members.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;This cemetery is located about 500 feet south of the Griffin Cemetery No. 1 on the bayou side. The property where the cemetery is located bel
2 CONC onged to Mrs. Joseph Authement.&amp;quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Among the members of the Louis Carroll Walker Crosby family listed as having been buried there are Isaac George Griffin; Laura Batistile Crosby; Louis Carroll Th
2 CONC omas Crosby II [&lt;em&gt;sic&lt;/em&gt;]; Eveline Marie Dantin; Eulalie Adrienne Crosby. The name Louis Carroll Thomas Crosby II, above, is evidently meant to be the Louis Carroll Crosby who was born in 1817 and died in 1887. His obituary states t
2 CONC hat his full name was Louis Carroll Walkker Crosby. While no records have been found of his baptism, marriages, or death, it is clear from the baptism records of his children that he is not the same person as his son who was baptized as Louis Carro
2 CONC ll Thomas Crosby on 3 August 1855 and who styled himself as Louis Carroll Crosby, Jr. This son was born in 1851 and died in 1891, and it is not certain that he is buried in this cemetery.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
